  "details": "I don't know if this is the place for this feedback. So it's time for a gamble.\n\nI think it's time to have a think about how thumbnails are shown to the user. Right now images gets stretched, cut off and squished depending on where you look. And I personally find it kind of messy at the moment.\n\nI've provided some examples on how it's shown in different places. Where it's a good mix between 4:3 and 1:1 frames. The most pictures are on the same avatar that is uploaded with the tool on the website that crops images to 1:1.\n\nThe cropping in the recently used list makes sense. Just added it since it's one more way.\n\nI could only find one example for worlds. And that is that it's squished in the menu wing.\n\nI have one avatar with a 4:3 image on a pedestal. And that gets squished to 1:1 instead. So 4:3 is not a 100% solution either.\n\nI just wish it was more consistent. Ans less stretch etc. I'd personally go for just keeping an images ratio in the menus/website and just put a background on it if it doesn't fit nicely.",
